        "title": "Introduction",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Suppose that we want to factor the following trinomial:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: t^4+4t^2+3.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Suppose that we want to factor the following trinomial:\n[MATH: t^4+4t^2+3.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>This trinomial is a quartic, but it can also be viewed as a quadratic &quot;in disguise.&quot; To see this, notice that if we introduce a new variable <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=t^2,]</span> then we can rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "This trinomial is a quartic, but it can also be viewed as a quadratic \"in disguise.\" To see this, notice that if we introduce a new variable [MATH: z=t^2,] then we can rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|=; (t^{2})^{2} + 4(t^{2}) + 3|=; z^{2} + 4z + 3]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|=; (t^{2})^{2} + 4(t^{2}) + 3|=; z^{2} + 4z + 3]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Now, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: t\\mathbin{:}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Now, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: t\\mathbin{:}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: z^{2} + 4z + 3|=; (z + 1)(z + 3)|=; (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: z^{2} + 4z + 3|=; (z + 1)(z + 3)|=; (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, <span class=\"math\">[MATH: t^4+4t^2+3]</span> factors into <span class=\"math\">[MATH: (t^2+1)(t^2+3).]</span> We can double-check this result by multiplying it out:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, [MATH: t^4+4t^2+3] factors into [MATH: (t^2+1)(t^2+3).] We can double-check this result by multiplying it out:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{2}(t^{2} + 3) + 1(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{4} + 3t^{2} + t^{2} + 3|=; t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|\u2713]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{2}(t^{2} + 3) + 1(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{4} + 3t^{2} + t^{2} + 3|=; t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|\u2713]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nSuppose that we want to factor the following trinomial:\n[MATH: t^4+4t^2+3.]\n\nContent:\nThis trinomial is a quartic, but it can also be viewed as a quadratic \"in disguise.\" To see this, notice that if we introduce a new variable [MATH: z=t^2,] then we can rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|=; (t^{2})^{2} + 4(t^{2}) + 3|=; z^{2} + 4z + 3]\n\nContent:\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: t\\mathbin{:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: z^{2} + 4z + 3|=; (z + 1)(z + 3)|=; (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, [MATH: t^4+4t^2+3] factors into [MATH: (t^2+1)(t^2+3).] We can double-check this result by multiplying it out:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{2}(t^{2} + 3) + 1(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{4} + 3t^{2} + t^{2} + 3|=; t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|\u2713]"
      },
