          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Factor <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^4-4x^2+4.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Factor [MATH: x^4-4x^2+4.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We can introduce a new variable <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z=x^2]</span> and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: x^{4} \u2212 4x^{2} + 4|=; (x^{2})^{2} \u2212 4(x^{2}) + 4|=; z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4]</span></p><p>Now, we can factor the quadratic as the square of a difference, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4|=; (z \u2212 2)^{2}|=; (x^{2} \u2212 2)^{2}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We can introduce a new variable [MATH: z=x^2] and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: x^{4} \u2212 4x^{2} + 4|=; (x^{2})^{2} \u2212 4(x^{2}) + 4|=; z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4]\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic as the square of a difference, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: x\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4|=; (z \u2212 2)^{2}|=; (x^{2} \u2212 2)^{2}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nFactor [MATH: x^4-4x^2+4.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe can introduce a new variable [MATH: z=x^2] and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: x^{4} \u2212 4x^{2} + 4|=; (x^{2})^{2} \u2212 4(x^{2}) + 4|=; z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4]\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic as the square of a difference, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: x\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4|=; (z \u2212 2)^{2}|=; (x^{2} \u2212 2)^{2}]"
      },
