    "readable_text": "Item 1 \u2014 Tutorial: Introduction\n\nContent:\nSuppose that we want to factor the following trinomial:\n[MATH: t^4+4t^2+3.]\n\nContent:\nThis trinomial is a quartic, but it can also be viewed as a quadratic \"in disguise.\" To see this, notice that if we introduce a new variable [MATH: z=t^2,] then we can rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|=; (t^{2})^{2} + 4(t^{2}) + 3|=; z^{2} + 4z + 3]\n\nContent:\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: t\\mathbin{:}]\n\nContent:\n[MATH: z^{2} + 4z + 3|=; (z + 1)(z + 3)|=; (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)]\n\nContent:\nTherefore, [MATH: t^4+4t^2+3] factors into [MATH: (t^2+1)(t^2+3).] We can double-check this result by multiplying it out:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{2}(t^{2} + 3) + 1(t^{2} + 3)|=; t^{4} + 3t^{2} + t^{2} + 3|=; t^{4} + 4t^{2} + 3|\u2713]\n\n---\n\nItem 2 \u2014 Example: Factoring Biquadratic Expressions as Perfect Squares\n\nExample Prompt:\nFactor [MATH: x^4-4x^2+4.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe can introduce a new variable [MATH: z=x^2] and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: x^{4} \u2212 4x^{2} + 4|=; (x^{2})^{2} \u2212 4(x^{2}) + 4|=; z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4]\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic as the square of a difference, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: x\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: z^{2} \u2212 4z + 4|=; (z \u2212 2)^{2}|=; (x^{2} \u2212 2)^{2}]\n\n---\n\nItem 3 \u2014 Question 1\n\nPrompt:\nFactor [MATH: 4x^{4} + 4x^{2} + 1.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (x^{2} + 2)^{2}]\nb. [MATH: (x + 1)^{4}]\nc. [MATH: (4x^{2} + 1)^{2}]\nd. [MATH: (2x^{2} + 1)^{2}]\ne. [MATH: (2x + 1)^{4}]\n\n---\n\nItem 4 \u2014 Question 2\n\nPrompt:\nFactor [MATH: y^{4} + 6y^{2} + 9.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (y^{2} \u2212 3)^{2}]\nb. [MATH: (y \u2212 3)^{2}]\nc. [MATH: (y^{2} + 3y)^{2}]\nd. [MATH: (y + 3)^{2}]\ne. [MATH: (y^{2} + 3)^{2}]\n\n---\n\nItem 5 \u2014 Example: Factoring Biquadratic Expressions as Quadratic Trinomials\n\nExample Prompt:\nFactor [MATH: t^4 - t^2 - 2.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe can introduce a new variable [MATH: z = t^2] and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: z\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: t^{4} \u2212 t^{2} \u2212 2|=; (t^{2})^{2} \u2212 t^{2} \u2212 2|=; z^{2} \u2212 z \u2212 2]\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: t\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: z^{2} \u2212 z \u2212 2|=; (z + 1)(z \u2212 2)|=; (t^{2} + 1)(t^{2} \u2212 2)]\n\n---\n\nItem 6 \u2014 Question 3\n\nPrompt:\nFactor [MATH: x^{4} \u2212 x^{2} \u2212 6.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (x^{2} \u2212 2)(x^{2} \u2212 3)]\nb. [MATH: (x^{2} \u2212 2)(x^{2} + 3)]\nc. [MATH: (x + 2)(x \u2212 3)]\nd. [MATH: (x \u2212 2)(x + 3)]\ne. [MATH: (x^{2} + 2)(x^{2} \u2212 3)]\n\n---\n\nItem 7 \u2014 Question 4\n\nPrompt:\nFactor [MATH: q^{4} + 5q^{2} + 6.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (q^{2} + 2)(q^{2} \u2212 3)]\nb. [MATH: (q^{2} \u2212 2)^{2}]\nc. [MATH: (q^{2} + 2)(q^{2} + 3)]\nd. [MATH: (q^{2} + 3)^{2}]\ne. [MATH: (q^{2} \u2212 2)(q^{2} \u2212 3)]\n\n---\n\nItem 8 \u2014 Example: Factoring Biquadratic Expressions as Quadratic Trinomials With Leading Coefficients\n\nExample Prompt:\nFactor [MATH: 2p^4 + 5p^2 + 3.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe can introduce a new variable [MATH: t = p^2] and then rewrite the trinomial as a quadratic in terms of [MATH: t\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 2p^{4} + 5p^{2} + 3|=; 2(p^{2})^{2} + 5p^{2} + 3|=; 2t^{2} + 5t + 3]\n\nNow, we can factor the quadratic, and then rewrite the final expression in terms of [MATH: p\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: 2t^{2} + 5t + 3|=; (t + 1)(2t + 3)|=; (p^{2} + 1)(2p^{2} + 3)]\n\n---\n\nItem 9 \u2014 Question 5\n\nPrompt:\nFactor [MATH: 2w^{4} + 9w^{2} \u2212 5.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (2w \u2212 1)(w + 5)]\nb. [MATH: (2w^{2} + 1)(w^{2} \u2212 5)]\nc. [MATH: (2w \u2212 1)(w^{2} + 5)]\nd. [MATH: (2w^{2} \u2212 1)(w^{2} + 5)]\ne. [MATH: 2(w^{2} \u2212 1)(w^{2} + 5)]\n\n---\n\nItem 10 \u2014 Question 6\n\nPrompt:\nFactor [MATH: 3y^{4} + 10y^{2} + 3.]\n\nChoices:\na. [MATH: (y^{2} + 1)(3y^{2} + 2)]\nb. [MATH: (3y + 1)^{4}]\nc. [MATH: (2y + 3)^{4}]\nd. [MATH: (y^{2} + 2)(3y^{2} + 1)]\ne. [MATH: (y^{2} + 3)(3y^{2} + 1)]"
